Evidence: Gates

Purpose:
  Defines evidence requirements for gate results.

EvidenceRequirements:
  Every gate result MUST include:
    - Who ran the gate
    - What was tested
    - When it was run
    - Why it was run
    - Result (PASS/FAIL/BLOCKED/etc.)
    - Evidence artifact

EvidenceTypes:
  BDD-GATE:
    test result
  SECURITY-GATE:
    SAST report
  LOAD-GATE:
    k6 report
  DEPLOY-GATE:
    deployment result
  PENTEST-GATE:
    pentest report
  MANUAL-QA-GATE:
    manual test result

EvidenceStorage:
  Artifacts stored in:
    .sdd/.runtime/cache/

  References stored in:
    .sdd/gates/evidence/

EvidenceRules:
  [EV1]  Every gate MUST produce evidence.
  [EV2]  Evidence MUST be immutable after gate completion.
  [EV3]  Evidence MUST be linkable from graph.
  [EV4]  Evidence MUST be retrievable for audit.

GateAudit:
  Format:
    Gate: <gate-id>
    Who: <actor>
    What: <action>
    When: <timestamp>
    Why: <reason>
    Result: <PASS/FAIL/BLOCKED>
    Evidence: <artifact-reference>

State: +
  